          <title data-react-helmet="true">Crispy Cauliflower Tacos</title>
          <meta data-react-helmet="true" name="description" content="We&#x27;ll eat cauliflower in any form—whole roasted, on sliders, as a rice substitute.Add to that list these crispy cauliflower tacos. We bake florets to perfection (it&#x27;s all about the seasoning), drizzle them with queso (homemade, duh) and wrap everything in warm tortillas (we used the flour variety). We have a feeling you&#x27;re going to like—wait, scratch that—love the final result."/><meta data-react-helmet="true" property="og:url" content="https://www.purewow.com/recipes/crispy-cauliflower-tacos-recipe"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" property="og:type" content="article"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" property="og:title" content="Crispy Cauliflower Tacos"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" property="og:image" content="https://assets.purewow.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/caulitaco-400.png"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" property="og:image:width" content="600px"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" property="og:image:height" content="300px"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" property="og:description" content="We&#x27;ll eat cauliflower in any form—whole roasted, on sliders, as a rice substitute.Add to that list these crispy cauliflower tacos. We bake florets to perfection (it&#x27;s all about the seasoning), drizzle them with queso (homemade, duh) and wrap everything in warm tortillas (we used the flour variety). We have a feeling you&#x27;re going to like—wait, scratch that—love the final result."/><meta data-react-helmet="true" property="og:updated_time" content="2016-09-08T07:00:00-04:00"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" name="twitter:title" content="Crispy Cauliflower Tacos"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" name="twitter:image:src" content="https://assets.purewow.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/09/caulitaco-400.png"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" name="twitter:site" content="@PureWow"/><meta data-react-helmet="true" 